            <ArticleTitle>[The electrocardiogram characteristics of patients with ischemic heart disease combined with spinal osteochondrosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study in presented of 25 patients with exertion stenocardia (class II-III) in association with cervicothoracic osteochondrosis. The authors established the diagnostic value of vertebral load tests in the differentiation of vertebra-dependent changes of the electrocardiogram in case of association of ischemic heart disease with osteochondrosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
